From 3e5adcf09230677083433620bcd92ad363dab00f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:18:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: j716s: Build in netconsole and ramoops

The J716s has no serial console, and a boot that hangs or panics before
the network is up leaves no record.

NETCONSOLE with NETCONSOLE_DYNAMIC lets userspace point a target at the
USB Ethernet adapter once it is up. netconsole= on the command line
cannot: the adapter appears about 3 s into the boot. This is the route
that works on this machine: lines printed before a panic get out, and
with an adapter whose driver sends directly (AX88179) the panic too.

PANIC_TIMEOUT=10 restarts a panicked kernel after 10 s instead of
leaving it to the boot loader's watchdog, or spinning forever when
nothing armed one.

PSTORE_RAM was =m and the root loads no modules. It is built in, with
the console and pmsg front ends (ftrace off), for a loader that supplies
a ramoops node; the device tree carries none. On the J716s no RAM region
survives a reset today: iBoot initialises the (ECC) DRAM again at every
boot, and clears its /pram panic-log region too, so a ramoops region in
either came back empty after a warm reboot and after a panic. With no
node, ramoops stays idle.

Against defconfig + asahi.config + j716s.config this changes those
symbols and what they select: NETPOLL, NET_POLL_CONTROLLER,
PRINTK_EXECUTION_CTX, and REED_SOLOMON from =m to =y.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config b/arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config
index a2caebaa0399..d011225f5d69 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/j716s.config
@@ -132,6 +132,22 @@ CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG=y
 # runs the suspend path and resumes on its own after 5 s
 CONFIG_PM_DEBUG=y
 
+# Crash logs (no serial console). netconsole streams
+# the log over the USB Ethernet adapter once userspace has configured a
+# target through configfs (the adapter appears too late for netconsole=).
+# A panic restarts after 10 s instead of waiting for the watchdog.
+# pstore/ramoops is built in for a loader that supplies a ramoops node; the
+# DT has none, since iBoot clears both ordinary DRAM and its /pram region at
+# every boot, so nothing in RAM survives a reset on this machine today.
+CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM=y
+CONFIG_PSTORE_CONSOLE=y
+CONFIG_PSTORE_PMSG=y
+# CONFIG_PSTORE_FTRACE is not set
+CONFIG_NETCONSOLE=y
+CONFIG_NETCONSOLE_DYNAMIC=y
+CONFIG_PRINTK_TIME=y
+CONFIG_PANIC_TIMEOUT=10
+
 # Userspace: pacman's download sandbox, compressed swap, /dev/mem
 CONFIG_SECURITY_LANDLOCK=y
 CONFIG_ZRAM=y
-- 
